  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Deepak vs Sanjeev Kumar on 18 March, 2024 Author: Prem Narayan Singh Bench: Prem Narayan Singh 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore BEFORE HON'BLE SHRI JUSTICE PREM NARAYAN SINGH ON THE 18 th OF MARCH, 2024 CRIMINAL REVISION No. 5310 of 2019 BETWEEN:- 1. DEEPAK S/O ASHOK SANMUKHANI, AGED ABOUT 36 YEARS , OCCUPATION: BUSINESS 6/9 INDUSTRIAL AREA MAXI ROAD UJJAIN (MADHYA PRADESH) 2. NEERAJ S/ O SHRI ASHOK KANMUKHANI, AGED ABOUT 33 YEARS, OCCUPATION: BUSINESS 6/9 INDUSTRIAL AREA MAXI ROAD UJJAIN (MADHYA PRADESH) (BY NONE ) AND S A N J E E V KUMAR OCCUPATION: FOOD SAFETY OFFICER KHAD EVAM AUSHADI PRASHASAN DHAR (MADHYA PRADESH) .. (BY NONE ) Th is revision coming on for hearing this day, th e cour following: Deepak vs Sanjeev Kumar on 18 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97750928/ 1",
    "facts": "ORDER This petition has been filed under Section 397 of Cr.P.C. against the order of learned Sessions Judge wherein the learned Special Judge , District Dhar has allowed the appeal filed by the petitioners and reduced the fine amount of the petitioners from Rs.75,000/- each to Rs.5000/- each under Section 26(20(ii) and 27 r/w Section 52 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
